        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Czesław Miłosz, Nathalie Sarraute\n- Works: The Captive Mind\n- Roles: poet, prose writer, translator, diplomat, lawyer, writer, academic, Nobel laureate\n- Publishers: Secker and Warburg\n\nFacts:\n- Nathalie Sarraute was born on July 18, 1900, and she was a French lawyer and writer.\n- Czesław Miłosz was born on 30 June 1911, and he was a Polish poet, prose writer, translator, and diplomat.\n- The Captive Mind is a 1953 work of nonfiction by Czesław Miłosz.\n- The English translation of The Captive Mind was originally published by Secker and Warburg.\n- Czesław Miłosz was also an academic and a Nobel laureate.\n- Nathalie Sarraute died on October 19, 1999.\n- Czesław Miłosz died on 14 August 2004.",
